From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram -cells and -name
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

-cells {role master ...} picks the cell for a role (inv, and2, buffer,
clock_gate, aoi22, ao22, or2, nand2, nor2, tie, addr_flop) instead of
the smallest the libraries have of its function. On asap7 the smallest
are the xp cells a flow marks dont_use (INVxp33, AOI22xp33), and the
smallest buffer is the hold buffer HB1xp67; a core the parent keeps
fixed cannot be resized after. An AOI22 or AO22 given is checked by its
truth table, and its pins are read from it; findMaster4 now reads them
from the cell it picks, not from the last that matched in the search.

-name names the block and the behavioral model, instead of
RAM<words>x<bits>, so two RAMs of one size can live in one design.

Tested: src/ram/test/cells_name_asap7.tcl.

Commit 10 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
